// Demonstrates: a recognized command with a malformed internal expression — "set" needs an
// assignment ("$x = ..."), a bare variable reference isn't one. Two independent instances, to
// prove the parser recovers from the first and still catches the second (this error site
// resynchronizes differently from an unrecognized command name: readCommandContent() already
// consumes through this command's own ">>" before the assignment check runs, so no explicit skip
// is needed — or should be added — at the call site).
title: Start
speaker: Narrator
---
<<set $x>>
<<set $y>>
===
